  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ford Motor has $619M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Ford Motor won 16,399 awards with an average award size of $37.7K. Ford Motor obligations are up 30.5% year over year. Ford Motor obligations by fiscal year show: FY21 $503M, FY22 $688M, FY23 $307M, FY24 $580M, FY25 $474M, and FY26 $619M. Ford Motor received $619M from the General Services Administration among top buying agencies. Ford Motor obligations are concentrated in Automobile Manufacturing at $619M among top markets. Ford Motor current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations. Ford Motor activity reflects many small awards combined with large agency relationships concentrated in Automobile Manufacturing and the General Services Administration.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is Ford Motor's federal contracting footprint?",
        "body": "Ford Motor has $619M in obligations for FY2026 to date and 16,399 awards with an average award size of $37.7K. Ford Motor obligations are concentrated in Automobile Manufacturing at $619M and the General Services Administration is the top buyer at $619M. Ford Motor current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Ford Motor obligations moved over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Ford Motor obligations were $503M in FY21, $688M in FY22, $307M in FY23, $580M in FY24, $474M in FY25, and $619M in FY26. Ford Motor obligations are up 30.5% year over year in the current fiscal year to date. Ford Motor numbers show variability across years, with FY22 the highest of the listed years and FY23 the lowest."
      }
